			"note": "Real vim leaves the caret on the replacement (ch 1). The core computes the caret as `curEnd - 1` from the range it asked for (its surrogate-pair bump, ch 3) rather than the wider range the grapheme clamp actually replaced, so the caret lands one character further on. The text is right; only the caret differs, and only on a multi-codepoint cluster."
